From 5f095819af3091c442eb93cb9b0f88564b157b62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arsalan Naeem <naeemarsalan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:09:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov5693: set MIPI_CTRL00 clock-lane gate for IPU6
 front cameras

The mainline ov5693 driver never writes MIPI_CTRL00 (register 0x4800),
leaving it at its 0x00 power-on default. The IPU3 ISP, where this sensor
is the front camera of the Surface Pro 5/6/7, accepts that default. On
the IPU6 Surface devices (Surface Pro 8 and 9, Surface Go 4) the MIPI
D-PHY does not lock onto the link: the sensor reports streaming, but the
receiver never gets any CSI-2 packets and capture times out ("stream stop
time out").

The Windows driver programs 0x2d into this register. Bit sweeps on the
Surface Pro 8 and Surface Pro 9 showed that bit 5 (clock-lane gate) is
both necessary and sufficient, so set only that bit, with a
read-modify-write, before stream-on.

Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/pull/2171
Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/issues/1893
Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface/issues/2154
Signed-off-by: Arsalan Naeem <naeemarsalan@gmail.com>
[linux-cachyos-surface: ported to 7.2.9 and reduced from writing 0x2d to
 setting bit 5 only, as found on the Surface Pro 9 in the PR thread and
 as done by the linux-media submission]
Patchset: cameras
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
index 02236f3db..e815e6d8a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
@@ -110,6 +110,10 @@
 #define OV5693_MIN_CROP_WIDTH			2
 #define OV5693_MIN_CROP_HEIGHT			2
 
+/* MIPI control */
+#define OV5693_MIPI_CTRL00_REG			CCI_REG8(0x4800)
+#define OV5693_MIPI_CTRL00_CLK_LANE_GATE	BIT(5)
+
 /* Test Pattern */
 #define OV5693_TEST_PATTERN_REG			CCI_REG8(0x5e00)
 #define OV5693_TEST_PATTERN_ENABLE		BIT(7)
@@ -611,6 +615,19 @@ static int ov5693_enable_streaming(struct ov5693_device *ov5693, bool enable)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Set the CSI-2 clock-lane gate bit of MIPI_CTRL00 before starting the
+	 * stream. With the 0x00 power-on default the IPU3 receiver (Surface Pro
+	 * 5-7) locks onto the link, but the IPU6 D-PHY on the Surface Pro 8/9
+	 * and Surface Go 4 does not: the sensor streams while the receiver gets
+	 * no CSI-2 data and capture times out. Only this bit is needed, so
+	 * update it rather than overwriting the whole register.
+	 */
+	if (enable)
+		cci_update_bits(ov5693->regmap, OV5693_MIPI_CTRL00_REG,
+				OV5693_MIPI_CTRL00_CLK_LANE_GATE,
+				OV5693_MIPI_CTRL00_CLK_LANE_GATE, &ret);
+
 	cci_write(ov5693->regmap, OV5693_SW_STREAM_REG,
 		  enable ? OV5693_START_STREAMING : OV5693_STOP_STREAMING,
 		  &ret);
